{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he shall slaughter, and the priests shall offer.</b> From receiving and onward is the domain of priesthood — this teaches about slaughter that it is valid by a non-priest (there)." "<b>Before YHWH.</b> In the courtyard." "<b>And they shall offer.</b> This is receiving, for it is the first, and its meaning is a term of bringing — we have learned both of them." "<b>The sons of Aharon.</b> One might say disqualified ones — Scripture says, 'the priests.'" "<b>The blood, and sprinkle the blood.</b> Why does Scripture say 'blood' twice? To include that which became mixed in its own kind or in a different kind. One might say even with disqualified ones, or with inner sin-offerings, or with outer sin-offerings — for these are applied above and it is applied below — Scripture says, 'its blood in another place' (Zevachim 1)." "<b>And he shall sprinkle.</b> He stands below and sprinkles from the vessel at the wall of the altar, below the חוּט הַסִּקְרָא, at the corners — therefore סָבִיב is stated, that the blood should be placed on the four sides of the altar. Or could he go around it like a thread? Scripture says וְזָרְקוּ — and it is impossible to go around in sprinkling. If וְזָרְקוּ — could it be one sprinkling? Scripture says סָבִיב. How so? He gives two gifts that are four (Sifra)." "<b>That is at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> And not at a time when it is dismantled (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:39.948219752Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}